format session-log-v1
stamp 20260815.003415
editor Zed
model Fable 5
voice Kyri
host Ubuntu cloud pier — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title ALES105 — Lotus's invert, flip every sample's sign, the exact value-mirror of ALES104's reverse
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; after ALES104 sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think ALES104's own recommend line named invert as the next exact-and-structural crux, and it is the right one: reverse changes every POSITION and no value; invert is its exact twin from the other axis — every VALUE and no position, y = -x. It is the Invert / Invert Phase menu item every editor ships and earns real reach (two mics on one source brought into agreement, a difference signal cancelled, a stereo side folded). No invert.rye existed; it stays perfectly exact off the signed rail, so it keeps the ALES ladder's exact-law discipline rather than the tolerance a decibel/RMS rung would need.
think Shape: invert(clip), no parameter, no fault from legal input. Walk the clip once and write saturate(-x) into each seat — one in-place pass of len writes, no allocation, no second buffer. Crucially it REUSES ALES2's timeline.saturate, the same clamp gain already uses, so the one non-exact sample (sample_min, whose true negation +32768 is out of i16 range) is pinned to sample_max in exactly one place across the suite, never re-derived and never wrapped.
think The honesty this rung owes is the two's-complement rail. Reverse is a perfect involution; invert is an involution ONLY on [sample_min+1, sample_max]. sample_min (-32768) has no positive twin: invert(-32768) = 32767, invert(32767) = -32767, so a floor seat round-trips to -32767, not -32768. I stated this as its own law rather than hiding it — the involution law WITH AN HONEST RAIL — and proved it both ways: a clip free of the floor round-trips to the byte, a clip holding the floor round-trips to -32767 at exactly those seats.
think Four laws, all provable: the VALUE-MIRROR law (invert lands a hand-inverted vector exactly, the floor and the ceiling both riding along); the INVOLUTION law with the honest rail (off-rail identity over five clips including single-sample and empty; on-rail pinned to -32767); the MAGNITUDE law (off the rail |−x| = |x|, so the peak re-measured through ALES13 is unchanged, length unchanged too); the FIXPOINT law (zero the unique fixed point of negation — the all-zero and empty clips each their own invert).
obs Witness GREEN on the first pass — value-mirror on [10,-20,0,100,-100,32767,-32768] landing [-10,20,0,-100,100,-32767,32767] (the floor saturating to sample_max); off-rail involution over five clips; on-rail double-invert pinning the two -32768 seats to -32767 while 500 and -1 round-trip exact; magnitude over three clips checking length and re-measured peak unchanged; fixpoint on empty and all-zero. TAME style bans clean (ratchet zero-assert count unchanged at 11); >=2 asserts per fn, invariants stated positively; the Clip, saturate, and the ALES13 meter reused whole, no new arithmetic invented.
obs No custody gate reached — software only, local; it flips existing samples about zero and fabricates none, changes no length, reads no byte past len; no funds, keys, network, device, or real speaker.
loom witness=ales_invert_witness green=1 laws=4 writes=len module_bytes=8k rail_exception=sample_min
file lotus/invert.rye ALES105 — invert() writes saturate(-x) into each seat, len writes in place; reuses timeline.saturate for the rail; postcondition asserts the length is unchanged.
file tools/ales_invert_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs the selftest, asserts the GREEN line.
file active-designing/20260815-003415_fill-ales105-lotus-invert.md the self-approved design read naming the value-mirror, involution-with-rail, magnitude, and fixpoint laws.
file lotus/README.md front door — the ALES105 rung added to the roster status line and a full bullet beside ALES104's mirror.
recommend keep-going — the next Lotus crux stays exact and structural: a rotate/shift that reseats the clip around a point (its own inverse a counter-rotate), a per-region reverse or invert over an ALES23 selection, or a swap-halves; each its own self-approved round, no custody gate reached.
